{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1259086-martial-arts-boxing","id":1259086,"title":"Martial Arts & Boxing","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-10-05T08:18:40-07:00","id":1259086,"title":"Martial Arts & Boxing","content":"Hello :-)<br /> <br /> Whirlwind Strike (Martial Arts 3), Defensive Jab (Boxing 2), and Combination (Boxing 4) all provide different methods of dealing additional damage in combat.<br /> <br /> The Hand as Weapon (Martial Arts 4) makes your unarmed strikes do Letha.<br /> The Touch of Death (Martial Arts 5) makes your hands a 2 Damage Rating weapon.<br /> <br /> So, if someone has Martial Arts 4 and 5, would the extra damage from Martial Arts 3, Boxing 2, and Boxing 4 follow suit? Or are they still considered Bashing Damage despite the mechanics of Martial Arts 4 and 5? (ie: are the various sources of damage upgraded to Lethal, with an additional 2 damage on a successful hit?)<br /> <br /> Thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The best lies are wrapped in truth.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11526-lasellj","name":"lasellj","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11526_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-05T12:35:34-07:00","id":1259112,"title":"","content":"Martial Arts 3 and Boxing 2 don't get upgrades from MA 4 or 5. They deal bashing damage based on opponent actions, not your unarmed strikes.<br /> <br /> You can definitely combine MA 4 and Boxing 4 for a lethal damage strike with extra damage on a successful hit. MA 5 and Boxing 4 should also stack by my reading of the Hurt Locker stacking guidelines (they both make the attack do more damage, but one is a flat damage increase and the other is bonus dice), but there's a judgemental call to make there and some people might disagree validly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}